    "['route-policy [parameter1] permit node [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set policy-options policy-statement 2 term 2 from route-filter 192.168.1.0/24 exact', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set policy-options policy-statement 2 term 2 from route-filter 192.168.1.0/24 exact', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Juniper configuration for the given Huawei `route-policy` command:\\n\\n##\\nset policy-options policy-statement 2 term 2 from route-filter 192.168.1.0/24 exact\\nset policy-options policy-statement 2 term 2 from route-filter 192.168.2.0/24 exact\\nset policy-options policy-statement 2 term 2 then accept\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- Juniper uses `policy-statement` instead of `route-policy`\\n- The `term` in Juniper is equivalent to `node` in Huawei\\n- The ACL matching is translated to `route-filter` statements\\n- The `permit` action becomes `then accept`\\n- Both source networks from ACL 2001 are included as separate filters\\n- The `exact` modifier ensures the same behavior as Huawei's 0.0.0.255 wildcard mask (which matches exact /24 prefixes)\", 'trans_template': 'set policy-options policy-statement 2 term 2 from route-filter 192.168.1.0/24 exact'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set policy-options policy-statement 2 term 2 from route-filter 192.168.2.0/24 exact', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set policy-options policy-statement 2 term 2 from route-filter 192.168.2.0/24 exact', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Juniper configuration for the given Huawei `route-policy` command:\\n\\n##\\nset policy-options policy-statement 2 term 2 from route-filter 192.168.1.0/24 exact\\nset policy-options policy-statement 2 term 2 from route-filter 192.168.2.0/24 exact\\nset policy-options policy-statement 2 term 2 then accept\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- Juniper uses `policy-statement` instead of `route-policy`\\n- The `term` in Juniper is equivalent to `node` in Huawei\\n- The ACL matching is transl