    "['tunnel-protocol [parameter1] [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel encapsulation gre', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Juniper equivalent command for `tunnel-protocol gre p2mp`:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel encapsulation gre\\nset interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel multipoint\\n##\\n\\nNote:\\n1. Juniper uses `gr-` (GRE) interface naming by default for GRE tunnels\\n2. The `multipoint` parameter is added to enable point-to-multipoint functionality\\n3. In Juniper, you would typically create a logical unit (unit 0) under the physical interface\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel encapsulation gre'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel multipoint', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Juniper equivalent command for `tunnel-protocol gre p2mp`:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel encapsulation gre\\nset interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel multipoint\\n##\\n\\nNote:\\n1. Juniper uses `gr-` (GRE) interface naming by default for GRE tunnels\\n2. The `multipoint` parameter is added to enable point-to-multipoint functionality\\n3. In Juniper, you would typically create a logical unit (unit 0) under the physical interface\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel multipoint'}]]": 1,
    "['source [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel source ge-1/0/0.0', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Juniper equivalent for the HUAWEI command `source GigabitEthernet1/0/0`:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel source ge-1/0/0.0\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. In Juniper, GRE tunnels are configured under `gr-0/0/0` interface (generic routing encapsulation)\\n2. The `tunnel source` parameter specifies the physical interface to use as the source\\n3. `ge-1/0/0.0` is the Juniper equivalent of HUAWEI's GigabitEthernet1/0/0 (with .0 indicating unit 0)\\n4. The command is placed under the GRE interface configuration context\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel source ge-1/0/0.0'}]]": 1,
